## How it works (as verified, not as assumed)
desktop:1 = Ubuntu 24.04 + Xvfb + XFCE + x11vnc + noVNC/websockify +
xdotool/wmctrl/scrot/xclip + Chrome, and the Claude Code, Codex, Pi,
OpenCode and Cursor CLIs. Per screen: Xvfb :N, XFCE, x11vnc on 5900+N
(-localhost -nopw), websockify on 6080+N with a TokenFile map.

Request path: control plane -> host agent-api (mTLS) -> guest agent on
the box IP:1028 behind an AUTH preface line -> argv exec of xdotool et
al with DISPLAY=:N. Not vsock; 1028 is the same channel exec/files use.

noVNC auth is a 64-hex bearer in the URL query, 1h TTL, rotated on every
connect. x11vnc is -nopw but -localhost, so that token is the only gate.
Ports 5900-5907 are refused by the tunnel path so raw RFB can't bypass
it. The websocket rides the generic ingress reverse proxy — there is no
VNC-specific component anywhere.

## Decisions
- Scope: both halves (human-facing URL + agent-facing computer use),
  chosen by the user over docs-only or either half alone.
- Dropped a first design that read the screen token out of
  /var/lib/fcspawn/computer-screens/screen-0.conf via `sandbox exec` and
  rebuilt the URL from ingress_url_template. Once the HTTP layer existed
  for computer-use, GET .../screens/screen-0/connect returns a complete
  `url` — that deleted the exec, the file parsing and the string
  building.
- Wrapped ~10 ops rather than all ~30 routes; `raw` covers the rest.
- No test file: the repo has no test harness, and the logic is HTTP
  plumbing that needs a live box. Adding bats for this would be the
  over-engineering the repo's own guidance cuts.

## Bugs found
- Mine, fixed before commit: api_auth() preferred an api key while the
  CLI prefers an OAuth session. With both credentials on disk the two
  paths can authenticate as different identities.
- Pre-existing, NOT fixed here: cos tells users to export
  CREATEOS_API_KEY and `cos auth` reports "signed in via
  CREATEOS_API_KEY", but that env var appears nowhere in createos-cli.
  A user with only that set passes the preflight, then every CLI-driven
  verb fails "you're not signed in". Needs a decision: add the env var
  to the CLI, or drop the claim from cos.

## Upstream gaps worth issues (fc-origin, per the mesh protocol)
- No desktop-readiness signal. Three clients now hand-roll the same
  poll: SDK example 55, this driver, and any future CLI.
- 409 desktop_unavailable conflates "still booting" with "the action
  failed on a live desktop". No client can disambiguate it.
- Public docs have no /computer REST page and no SDK reference entry.

Live verification used a real box which was destroyed afterwards. No
